triage: revise_rules: The game file works as specified, but the rules make passive play dominant. The 'first' policy, almost certainly always bidding the minimum of 0, wins about 88% of decided games: it keeps all 100 starting money and still collects payments as auctioneer, while paintings are capped at 60 and are often worth 0. The 'last' policy, bidding everything, loses badly, so in practice there is no real auction tension.
